- F-34 **Against the interpreter's library, on the code of `ba3c7c876d`, the code generator refuses 1 declaration of the fourteen components that the distance stage checks, a declaration that the checker passes; the count can be taken only on a patched tree.** The setting is the distance stage's (F-53): the checker's failures caught per declaration, and the bound `Any`. Without the patch, the code generator stops `FortressLibrary`, `FortressBuiltin` and `FlatString` whole at the wrappers of their helper classes (row 874), so the measure's script first patches a scratch worktree (`compile-ladder/plan-31/PROBES.md` gives the patch). Then: 1 refused, 753 emitted, no component failure. The one refused declaration is `FortressLibrary`'s `__bigOperator2`, a generic method called on a receiver typed by a type variable (row 1076). On the code of `d3747846c1` the count was 13 in 4 kinds, with 745 emitted; the other 12 stopped at varargs, in two kinds (row 624), or at a closure class written twice (row 315), and both rows are fixed since (F-390, F-389). On the code of `c3b16ef2d1` the count was 17 in 5 kinds, with 742 emitted. The sums differ from code to code, since the earlier files also counted as emitted an object that its pre-pass refused. A declaration counts at its first wall, and some hold a second. The measure skips the dispatch methods, and it sees no class that is emitted and fails when it loads. No emitted class of the measure is run, and no test checks the count, since the gate's distance stage runs no code generation. So after the switch-over the code generator still stands between the library and bytecode. Measured once on each code. Command: `explorations/compile-ladder/plan-31/probes/planner/codegen-measure.sh <scratch-worktree> <out-dir>`. Detail: `compile-ladder/plan-33/probes/measure-ba3c7c876d.txt`; `compile-ladder/plan-33/probes/measure-d3747846c1.txt`; `compile-ladder/plan-31/probes/planner/measure-c3b16ef2d1.txt`; `compile-ladder/plan-31/PROBES.md`, "3. The measure: the declarations of the fourteen components that the code generator refuses".
