- F-320 **The code generator compiles a block's local functions as closures, the group recursive and mutually recursive without a mutable cell.** Each local function of a block is a closure class made as a function expression's, bound under its name in the block's environment, so a call of it and its use as a value go through the closure; it reaches itself as its own `this` and each sibling through a field of its class that the block sets once, after the whole group is made and before the body runs (`compiler/codegen/CodeGen.java`). It refuses three forms that the specification allows, each after the checker passes the program, with its own message: a local function with static parameters of its own, two of one name in a block, and the `atomic` modifier (row 304); a varargs one stops at 'Can't compile VarArgs yet' against the compiler's prelude, which declares no `ImmutableArray`, and compiles under the selection of the one library (F-390). By F-34's measure on `dbf4825e0`'s code, taken once, all nine of the library's declarations that stopped at 'Can't compile LetFn' emit. Gated by `compiler_tests/LocalFunctionCallCompiled`, `LocalFunctionValueCompiled`, `LocalFunctionRecursiveCompiled`, `LocalFunctionCaptureCompiled` and `LocalFunctionGenericContextCompiled`, their `tests/LocalFunction*Walk` guards, and `XXXLocalFunctionGenericCompiled`, `XXXLocalFunctionOverloadedCompiled` and `XXXLocalFunctionAtomicCompiled`. Detail: `compile-ladder/rung-codegen-local-functions/REPORT.md` sections 1 and 5.
